{"id":4923,"date":"2018-08-17T09:36:12","date_gmt":"2018-08-17T13:36:12","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?p=4923"},"modified":"2018-08-17T09:36:12","modified_gmt":"2018-08-17T13:36:12","slug":"our-visit-to-the-gerald-r-ford-presidential-museum","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2018\/08\/17\/our-visit-to-the-gerald-r-ford-presidential-museum\/","title":{"rendered":"Our Visit to the Gerald R. Ford Presidential Museum"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>Spending our 2nd summer as Workampers at <a href=\"https:\/\/www.peremarquettervpark.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Pere Marquette Oaks RV Resort<\/a> in &#8220;Baldwin&#8221; Michigan, we again had the opportunity every few days to explore the area of what northwest Michigan has to offer.<\/p>\n<p>We&#8217;ve been working 7 days on duty, then 7 days off duty sharing responsibilities with our Workamper co-workers Russ and Mary.<\/p>\n<p>One day Kathy and I took a drive &#8220;down state&#8221; a little to Grand\u00a0Rapids to visit the Gerald R. Ford Presidential Museum and Burial Site of he and his wife Betty.<a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.15.50.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright size-medium wp-image-4928\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.15.50-300x169.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"300\" height=\"169\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.15.50-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.15.50-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.15.50-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.15.50.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/><\/a><\/p>\n<p>Gerald Rudolph Ford, Jr. was born on July 14, 1913.<\/p>\n<p>While Gerald Ford was still an infant, his parents were divorced, and his mother moved to\u00a0<a class=\"md-crosslink autoxref\" href=\"https:\/\/www.britannica.com\/place\/Grand-Rapids-Michigan\">Grand Rapids<\/a>, Michigan, where she married Gerald R. Ford, Sr., who adopted the boy and gave him his name.<\/p>\n<p>After graduating from the\u00a0<a class=\"md-crosslink\" href=\"https:\/\/www.britannica.com\/topic\/University-of-Michigan\">University of Michigan<\/a>\u00a0(1935), where he was a star gridiron-football player, Ford worked as an assistant coach while he earned a\u00a0<a class=\"md-crosslink autoxref\" href=\"https:\/\/www.britannica.com\/topic\/law\">law\u00a0<\/a>degree from\u00a0<a class=\"md-crosslink\" href=\"https:\/\/www.britannica.com\/topic\/Yale-University\">Yale University<\/a>\u00a0(1941). He joined the navy during\u00a0<a class=\"md-crosslink\" href=\"https:\/\/www.britannica.com\/event\/World-War-II\">World War II<\/a>\u00a0and served in the South Pacific, attaining the rank of lieutenant commander and nearly losing his life in 1944 during a deadly\u00a0<a class=\"md-crosslink autoxref\" href=\"https:\/\/www.britannica.com\/science\/typhoon-weather\">typhoon<\/a>\u00a0that killed hundreds.<\/p>\n<p>In 1948, the year he won his first elective office, as\u00a0<a class=\"md-crosslink\" href=\"https:\/\/www.britannica.com\/topic\/Republican-Party\">Republican<\/a>\u00a0congressman from Michigan, he married Elizabeth Anne Bloomer (<span id=\"ref1033609\"><\/span><a class=\"md-crosslink\" href=\"https:\/\/www.britannica.com\/biography\/Betty-Ford\">Betty Ford<\/a>), with whom he had four children\u2014three sons (Michael, John, and Steven) and one daughter (Susan).<\/p>\n<p>He served nearly 25 years as a\u00a0Representative\u00a0of\u00a0Michigan&#8217;s 5th congressional district, eight of them as the\u00a0Republican\u00a0Minority Leader. Serving from 1973 to 1974 as the 40th\u00a0Vice President of the United States, Ford was the first person appointed to the vice-presidency under the terms of the\u00a025th Amendment. He then became President upon\u00a0Richard Nixon&#8217;s resignation on August 9, 1974, and served until\u00a0January 20, 1977\u00a0as the 38th\u00a0President of the United States.<\/p>\n<p>Ford is the only President of the United States who was not elected by ballot for his terms as either President or Vice-President. (see below)<a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.14.18.jpg\"><br \/>\n<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-15.02.16.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-4929 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-15.02.16.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-15.02.16.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-15.02.16-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-15.02.16-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-15.02.16-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px\" \/><\/a><\/p>\n<p>The 44,000-square-foot two-story triangular museum is one of the highlights in a 20-acre park complex that includes the\u00a0<a title=\"Grand Rapids Public Museum\" href=\"https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Grand_Rapids_Public_Museum\">Grand Rapids Public Museum<\/a>\u00a0along the west bank of the Grand River in downtown Grand Rapids.<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong><em>Click on any of the pictures below to see a larger image with caption<\/em><\/strong><\/p>\n<div id='gallery-1' class='gallery galleryid-4923 gallery-columns-1 gallery-size-large'><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.15.00.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"385\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.15.00-1024x576.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-4930\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.15.00-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.15.00-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.15.00-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.15.00.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 685px) 100vw, 685px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-4930'>\n\t\t\t\tA symbol of Ford&#8217;s time on the University of Michigan football team\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.45.16.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"385\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.45.16-1024x576.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-4933\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.45.16-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.45.16-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.45.16-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.45.16.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 685px) 100vw, 685px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-4933'>\n\t\t\t\tThe desk from Ford&#8217;s congressional office\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.59.46.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"385\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.59.46-1024x576.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-4934\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.59.46-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.59.46-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.59.46-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-13.59.46.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 685px) 100vw, 685px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-4934'>\n\t\t\t\tA replica of the White House Oval Office during Ford&#8217;s presidency\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.00.00.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"385\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.00.00-1024x576.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.00.00-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.00.00-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.00.00-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.00.00.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 685px) 100vw, 685px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.26.32.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"385\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.26.32-1024x576.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-4936\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.26.32-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.26.32-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.26.32-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.26.32.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 685px) 100vw, 685px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-4936'>\n\t\t\t\tThe Cabinet Room\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.46.03.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"385\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.46.03-1024x576.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-4939\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.46.03-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.46.03-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.46.03-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.46.03.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 685px) 100vw, 685px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-4939'>\n\t\t\t\tBetty Ford&#8217;s Citizen&#8217;s Band (CB) Radio and her QSL card\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.51.11.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"385\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.51.11-1024x576.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-4940\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.51.11-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.51.11-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.51.11-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.51.11.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 685px) 100vw, 685px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-4940'>\n\t\t\t\tJust part of the museum displays\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.54.44.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"385\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.54.44-1024x576.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-4942\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.54.44-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.54.44-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.54.44-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-14.54.44.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 685px) 100vw, 685px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-4942'>\n\t\t\t\tA view of the pool from the 2nd floor of the museum\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-15.03.20.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"385\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-15.03.20-1024x576.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-4945\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-15.03.20-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-15.03.20-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-15.03.20-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-15.03.20.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 685px) 100vw, 685px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-4945'>\n\t\t\t\tLooking east from the museum across the Grand River to the Grand Rapids skyine\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-15.04.11.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"385\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-15.04.11-1024x576.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-4946\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-15.04.11-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-15.04.11-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-15.04.11-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/08\/2018-06-12-15.04.11.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 685px) 100vw, 685px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-4946'>\n\t\t\t\tOutside view of the 2 story triangular building\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\n<p>There&#8217;s so much to see and so much to read in this museum.\u00a0 There are lots of typed and hand written letters on display, audio and video recordings of the early years and his time as the leader of our nation, along with an entire display room dedicated to Betty Ford and her contributions to the community, the presidency,\u00a0 and the nation.<\/p>\n<p>Definitely could go back and spend the better part of an entire day taking in all the museum has to offer.<\/p>\n<p>Living the full-time RV lifestyle presents us with the wonderful opportunity to see and experience so much that we wouldn&#8217;t otherwise have had available to us.<\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Spending our 2nd summer as Workampers at Pere Marquette Oaks RV Resort in &#8220;Baldwin&#8221; Michigan, we again had the opportunity every few days to explore the area of what northwest Michigan has to offer. We&#8217;ve been working 7 days on duty, then 7 days off duty sharing responsibilities with our Workamper co-workers Russ and Mary. &hellip; <a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2018\/08\/17\/our-visit-to-the-gerald-r-ford-presidential-museum\/\" class=\"more-link\">Continue reading <span class=\"screen-reader-text\">Our Visit to the Gerald R. Ford Presidential Museum<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[264,19546,554707329,554707389],"tags":[554707586,554707588,554707587,554707582,554707585,11110,554707584,554707581,554707583,554707572],"class_list":["post-4923","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","hentry","category-learning","category-sightseeing","category-traveling","category-veterans","tag-betty-ford","tag-burial-site","tag-congress","tag-gerald-r-ford","tag-grand-rapids","tag-michigan","tag-presidency","tag-president","tag-united-states","tag-world-war-ii"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4923","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=4923"}],"version-history":[{"count":9,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4923\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":4953,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4923\/revisions\/4953"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=4923"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=4923"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=4923"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}